cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this computational scaffold, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Computational scaffold for the discriminant-12 Prym eigenform prototype"
authors:
  - family-names: Geblomi
    given-names: Heywood
repository-code: "https://github.com/HeywoodGeblomi/prym-eigenform-pipeline-d12"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Verified residual-0 real-multiplication projector, plane-preserving Rauzy
  generators, geometric construction of S(1,-2), constrained KZ integrator,
  and dual Rauzy path evaluation for the McMullen discriminant-12 Prym
  prototype. Individual non-tautological Lyapunov exponents are experimental.
  The sum 8/5 on H(4)^odd is due to Chen-Moller.
keywords:
  - Teichmuller dynamics
  - Prym eigenforms
  - Kontsevich-Zorich cocycle
  - Lyapunov exponents
  - translation surfaces
